		{
			"outputs":[
				
			],
			"color":"#432",
			"widgets_values":[
				"QUALITY-FIRST MODEL STACK\n==========================\nBase model  : minimax_h3_ref2va_bf16 (official full-precision Ref2VA)\nText encoder: qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_bf16\nVideo VAE   : minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16\nAudio VAE   : minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32\nLoRA        : h3-realism-people-t2v-i2v-r2v   strength 0.70\nSampling    : BasicScheduler beta + Euler, 20 steps, denoise 1.0\nResolution  : 1.4 MP, native single-pass long-take generation\n\nThe Turbo LoRA is intentionally removed for maximum detail and temporal quality.\nThe SageAttention patch remains visible but bypassed for vGPU compatibility.\nSingle-pass mode is retained because dual-pass context chains can introduce seams."
			],
			"inputs":[
				
			],
			"flags":{
				
			},
			"type":"Note",
			"mode":0,
			"bgcolor":"#653",
			"size":[
				430,
				150
			],
			"pos":[
				2575.114501953125,
				2182.365478515625
			],
			"id":32,
			"properties":{
				"ue_properties":{
					"widget_ue_connectable":{
						
					},
					"input_ue_unconnectable":{
						
					},
					"version":"7.8"
				},
				"widget_ue_connectable":{
					
				}
			},
			"order":5
		},
		{
			"outputs":[
				
			],
			"color":"#432",
			"widgets_values":[
				"H3 LONG TAKE — Motion Context V2 (local)\n==========================================\n\nSAMPLING\n  sampling_mode = single     <- NOT dual. This is the whole trick.\n  Tested: continuing a chain off dual-pass latents gives pixel shift at\n  the joins. Single pass joins clean. For long takes, always single.\n  1st_pass_only / disable_2nd_noise only affect the second pass.\n  In single mode they do nothing — leave them.\n\nQUALITY STEPS (green BasicScheduler node)\n  20  quality-first default for the BF16 base model without a Turbo LoRA\n  16  balanced alternative when generation time is more important\n  12  faster preview setting; use 20 for final output.\n\nRESOLUTION\n  1.0 MP  fast, safe default for iteration\n  1.4 MP  up to ~10 s per segment on a 24-32 GB card\n  Past ~1.2-1.4 MP you mostly buy size, not detail.\n  VRAM rule of thumb: frames x megapixels <= ~540 per segment.\n\nMULTI-TRACK EDITOR\n  Segment 1 = \"shot\".  Every later segment = \"context\".\n  ref_image_size = max\n  Put the reference image on segment 1 -> hover it -> Share icon ->\n  \"Use as shared reference\". Later segments inherit it automatically.\n\nPROJECT SETTINGS (Multi-Track Project node)\n  project_name          always name it (empty = \"default\")\n  segment_start_number  counts from 1\n  segment_count         -1 = from start segment to the end\n  Re-render ONE segment: start = N, count = 1  (local only —\n  the saved context latents live in output/easy_media/projects/<name>/)\n\nPROMPTS\n  - A context segment's timestamps land ~0.92 s early in the final\n    video (22 pinned frames are trimmed). Write T + 0.92 to land at T.\n  - Open every context segment with CONTINUATION only — same pace,\n    same camera, same light — and zero scenery nouns.\n  - Never carry a progressive camera move across a join.\n  - Put joins mid-walk / mid-climb, never on a doorway or threshold.\n  - Dialogue: ~one short line every 2.5 s. Split between sentences."
			],
			"inputs":[
				
			],
			"flags":{
				
